WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.400
This is the beginning of Volume 6, November 1, 1903. When the soul does all her actions

2
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.860
for the soul purpose of loving Jesus, she walks always in the daylight. It is never

3
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:28.340
nighttime for her. So walking in the daylight is John 8, 12, and John 9, 3. Jesus said,

4
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:36.100
"If you follow me, you will be walking in the daylight." So Louisa says, "Continue

5
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:42.860
in my usual state, I found myself outside of myself, and I saw myself as a little steamboat.

6
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:49.420
I was all surprised at seeing myself reduced to that shape. In the meantime, my adorable

7
00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:56.380
Jesus came and told me, "My daughter, the life of man is a steamboat. Here Jesus is

8
00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:03.940
using images of everyday life that are all around us." He will talk about electricity

9
00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:13.900
when they put electricity together, for example. And just as it is fire alone that allows the

10
00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:21.300
steamboat to move and the more lively and the bigger the fire the faster it runs, while

11
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:26.900
if the fire is small it moves at a slow pace, and if the fire is extinguished it remains

12
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:35.260
motionless, it's the same for the soul. If the fire of the love of God is big, it can

13
00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:41.060
be said that she flies above all things of the earth, and she always runs and flies

14
00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:53.260
towards her center, which is God. Now I want to give you God is love, 1 John 4 7. Our God

15
00:01:53.260 --> 00:02:06.340
is a consuming fire is Hebrews 12 29, and Deuteronomy 32 11 to 13 that we're walking

16
00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:11.900
with the Lord guiding us. If then the fire is small in her soul, it can be said that

17
00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:18.260
she walks with difficulty crawling and getting all muddy with everything of the earth. If

18
00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:23.780
then the fire is extinguished, she remains motionless without the life of God within

19
00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:31.140
herself. As though dead to all that is divine, that is the issue that the Lord is dealing

20
00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:39.260
with. You can be alive to the earth, but you can be dead to the things of God. And it's

21
00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:53.620
the alive to the things of God that are the important things. So then he said, "My daughter,

22
00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:59.540
when the soul does all of her actions, for the soul purpose of loving me," now in all

23
00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:06.020
of these writings, that's the only motivation that Jesus accepts, that we will do everything

24
00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:13.500
for love of him. And she wants no other recompense for her work, but my love alone, then she

25
00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:21.460
walks always in the daylight, because selfishness and self-interest are not going to be destroying

26
00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:28.660
things. It's never a night time for her. Even more, she walks within the sun itself. Now

27
00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:34.340
in these writings, the sun is a symbol of the divine will. So she walks within the Lord

28
00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:39.520
or within God herself, which almost like steam surrounds her to let her walk within

29
00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:46.160
herself, making her enjoy all the fullness of light. Not only this, but her very actions

30
00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:52.540
serve as light for her journey. Matthew 5, 17, Jesus tells us that we have to be light

31
00:03:52.540 --> 00:04:01.740
for the world. And so it increases for her new light all the time. Whenever we're relating

32
00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:10.780
to the Lord, he gives us new things all the time. So November the 8th, 1903, Jesus tells

33
00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:17.220
how the love of neighbor must be. Now the whole law and the prophets Jesus tells us in

34
00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:24.320
Matthew 22 hangs on love of God and love of neighbor. The whole 36 volumes of Louisa

35
00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:34.780
hangs on love of God and living in the divine will. So November the 8th, Louisa says, as

36
00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:41.300
I was in my usual state, I was praying for certain needs of other people. And blessed

37
00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:48.100
Jesus, moving in my interior told me, for what purpose are you praying for these people?

38
00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:54.780
In other words, why are you doing it? And Louisa said, Lord, and you, for what purpose

39
00:04:54.780 --> 00:05:01.380
did you love us? He said, I love you because you are my own thing. And when an object is

40
00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:09.020
one's own, one feels compelled to love it. It is like a necessity. So Louisa said, Lord,

41
00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:14.420
I am praying for these people because they are your own thing. Otherwise I would not

42
00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:20.140
have interested myself. And he placing his hand on my forehead, almost pressing it said,

43
00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:27.180
ah, it's because they are my own thing. This is how the love of neighbor should be all

44
00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:34.620
the time. That's Matthew 22 verses 37 to 40. That the love of neighbor, that we love them

45
00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:41.380
because they are God's. Now, as we go on, Louisa is going to say, but they are your

46
00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:50.420
images, Lord, in order to press home her point that she is loving and interceding for people

47
00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:57.940
who are not only belonging to the Lord, but they are in his own image. So November the

48
00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:07.660
10th, 1903, how true love forgets himself. Continuing in my usual state, Louisa said,

49
00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:15.220
I saw blessed Jesus for just a little saying to me, my daughter, true love forgets himself

50
00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:21.700
and lives out of the interests, the pains, and everything that belongs to the beloved.

51
00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:28.140
So that's Matthew 1624. If you truly love, you will live for the beloved. It's that

52
00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:36.460
simple. Someone who lives for themselves doesn't love. So Louisa said, Lord, how can one forget

53
00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:43.380
oneself when we feel ourselves so much? It's not something far away from us, you know,

54
00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:50.620
or separated, which can easily be forgotten. And again, Jesus added that that is precisely

55
00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:58.980
the sacrifice of true love, that while one has oneself, he must live out of everything

56
00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:04.420
that belongs to the beloved. So even though we're aware of our weaknesses and our sinfulness

57
00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:11.420
and all the rest of it, we don't stay there. We actually live out of the love of God. Even

58
00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:18.500
more. If he remembers himself, this memory must serve him to become more industrious about

59
00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:25.380
how to consume himself for the beloved object. So that means if the Lord loves somebody as

60
00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:31.320
weak and poor and miserable as me, then he deserves to be really served by someone who

61
00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:38.620
doesn't deserve to be his servant. And if the beloved sees that the soul gives all of

62
00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:45.380
herself to him, that's Deuteronomy six, chapter six, verses four to 10, that you would love

63
00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:50.780
the Lord with all your heart, with all your soul, with all your mind, and with all your

64
00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:59.220
being, note the all, not some of yourself, but all of yourself. So if the beloved sees

65
00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:04.900
that the soul gives all of herself to him, he will know well how to repay her by giving

66
00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:12.700
her all of himself. That's what the exchange is, this marvelous exchange that goes on between

67
00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:19.420
God and us, we give him everything he gives us everything. We get the better deal. He doesn't

68
00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:28.780
get much. So he he he repays by giving the soul all of himself and letting her live out

69
00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:37.580
of his divine life. That's a wonderful deal for us. So one who forgets himself completely

70
00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:42.020
finds everything. If you don't forget yourself completely, you're not in a position to find

71
00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:49.380
everything because you're occupied with the stuff you've held on to. Moreover, it is necessary

72
00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:57.540
to see the difference that exists between what one forgets and what one finds. If you find

73
00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:04.300
a diamond ring, you wouldn't mind throwing away something that was worthless. One forgets

74
00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:12.700
what is ugly and finds what is beautiful. One forgets nature and finds grace. One forgets

75
00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:20.780
passions and weaknesses understood and finds virtues and strengths understood. One forgets

76
00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:30.300
poverty and finds richness. One forgets foolishness and finds wisdom. One forgets the world and

77
00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:35.880
finds heaven. Now that whole section there should really be colored and underlined. It's

78
00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:46.860
one of the great gems of these writings. So November the 16th 1903. There's no sacrifice

79
00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:55.420
without denying oneself and sacrifice and denying oneself to rise to the most pure and

80
00:09:55.420 --> 00:10:05.220
perfect love. So you can't have any sacrifice without denying yourself and you need both

81
00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:10.420
sacrifice and denying yourself if you're to rise to the great love that the Lord is

82
00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:17.100
calling us to. So Louisa says, "This morning as I was outside of myself, I found myself

83
00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:23.340
with baby Jesus in my arms and with a virgin who laid me on the ground to make me suffer

84
00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:35.580
the crucifixion, not with nails but with fire, placing a charcoal fire on my hands and feet.

85
00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:41.500
Blessed Jesus was there assisting me while I was suffering and he said, "My daughter,

86
00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:50.140
there is no sacrifice without denying oneself." That's Matthew 1624. And Jesus says that this

87
00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:56.660
denial of oneself is for everybody, whether you're in the divine will or not. In other

88
00:10:56.660 --> 00:11:02.380
words, if you're living an ordinary spiritual life, the church has told us that this denial

89
00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:08.100
of self is absolutely essential. And if we don't deny ourselves, then divine love cannot

90
00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:15.500
be born in us. So there's no sacrifice without denying oneself. And sacrifice and denying

91
00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:26.380
oneself give rise to the most pure and perfect love that mark chapter 9 verse 49.

92
00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:35.020
And since sacrifice is sacred, it happens that it consecrates the soul to me as a sanctuary

93
00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:46.180
worthy of me to make of it my perpetual dwelling, 1 Corinthians 3 16. No, you're not that you

94
00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:54.180
are the temple of the living God and that God dwells in you. So let's sacrifice work

95
00:11:54.180 --> 00:12:02.100
in you and render your soul and body sacred so that everything may be sacred in you and

96
00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:09.060
consecrate everything to me. Now, this is all preparation for living in the divine will.

97
00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:16.020
We have to put aside the old self. We've got to put aside the demands of human nature.

98
00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:21.220
We've got to put aside our will in order that the divine will and the divine love will

99
00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:28.780
take over. If we don't do our part, there's nothing for the Lord to work with. So November

100
00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:36.300
the 19th 1903, while one is nothing, one can be all.

101
00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:42.580
Louisa says continuing in my usual state, I saw blessed Jesus in my interior and a light

102
00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:49.820
in my intellect. That means infused knowledge. She was given infused knowledge. So this light

103
00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:58.820
said, while one is nothing, one can be all. In other words, as ourselves, we are nothing.

104
00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:04.600
And in these writings, we have to acknowledge our nothingness and simply throw our nothingness

105
00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:12.260
into his allness so that he's completely free to work with us. But how? One becomes

106
00:13:12.260 --> 00:13:20.640
all through suffering, he says. Suffering makes the soul become pontiff, priest, king,

107
00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:30.580
prince, minister, judge, advocate, repairer, protector, and defender. That's some list.

108
00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:37.820
Notice that suffering has this extraordinary fruit in us. And since true suffering is the

109
00:13:37.820 --> 00:13:43.300
suffering wanted by God in the soul, not suffering that we bring on ourselves as a result of

110
00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:52.140
our sins, but suffering that the Lord has given to us. If the soul appeases or calms

111
00:13:52.140 --> 00:14:00.180
herself, that means she becomes reconciled to the divine will. And if she surrenders

112
00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:07.940
herself completely in God's will or God's holy volition, this appeasement or calming

113
00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:15.220
or surrender united to suffering allows the soul to rule over justice, to rule over the

114
00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:22.980
mercy of God, to rule over men and over all things. And that's called reigning with Christ.

115
00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:32.460
And that's Romans 5 17 that the Lord said that we could reign with him. Now, just as

116
00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:36.820
suffering gave Christ all the most beautiful qualities and all the honors and offices

117
00:14:36.820 --> 00:14:43.020
that the human nature can contain, in the same way by participating in the suffering

118
00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:50.180
of Christ, the soul participates in his qualities and in the honors and offices of Christ who

119
00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:56.940
is all. As the chart tells us, we will receive everything through him with him and in him.

120
00:14:56.940 --> 00:15:07.700
So I'll give you Philippians 4, 13, I can do all things in Christ. So we now come to

121
00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:17.500
November the 23rd, 1903. There is no beauty that equals suffering for God alone. Now,

122
00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:24.900
it doesn't say suffering, it says suffering for God alone. Louisa says, I felt impressed

123
00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:31.940
in my interior by what I had written above, as if it were not according to the truth.

124
00:15:31.940 --> 00:15:38.940
As soon as I saw blessed Jesus, I said, Lord, what I have written is not right. How can we

125
00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:45.380
have all of this through mere suffering? And Jesus said, my daughter, don't be surprised.

126
00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:52.380
Indeed, there is no beauty that equals suffering for the love of God alone. Notice he says,

127
00:15:52.380 --> 00:16:01.820
there's no beauty. We don't want to associate the word beauty with suffering at all. Two

128
00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:08.700
arrows come out of me continuously, one from the heart, which is love, and wounds all those

129
00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:18.460
who are on my lap. That means touches or penetrates. That is those who are in my grace. This arrow

130
00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:25.100
wounds, mortifies, heals, afflicts, attracts, reveals, consoles, and continues my passion

131
00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:31.900
and redemption in those who are on my lap. That means those in relationship with God.

132
00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:40.340
That this loving arrow of love that comes out from him has all of these different effects

133
00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:45.820
in us according to what is actually needed. Sometimes it mortifies us because we need

134
00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:51.020
to grow in humility or self-knowledge. Sometimes it heals us because that's the need. Sometimes

135
00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:56.220
it afflicts us because we need to maybe look at our consciences. Sometimes it attracts

136
00:16:56.220 --> 00:17:01.740
us to get us to come close to him. Sometimes it's revelation that gives us understanding

137
00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:07.860
of God's word and sometimes it consoles and sometimes it enables us to continue the passion

138
00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:15.420
of Christ. Now there's another arrow that comes from the heart of the Lord. The other

139
00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:23.180
one comes from my throne. And I entrusted to the angels who are my ministers. That's

140
00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:31.380
Hebrews 114, angels as the ministers of God. And they make this arrow flow over any kind

141
00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:38.260
of people chastising them and exciting all to conversion. Now throughout the book of

142
00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:47.380
Revelation from as soon as you get into the chastisement around chapter 6, you'll find

143
00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:53.020
that it is the angels who are carrying out God's orders from heaven and they carry them

144
00:17:53.020 --> 00:18:00.140
out upon the earth. Now while he was saying this, Jesus shared his pains with me, telling

145
00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:07.260
me here in you also is the continuation of my redemption, that is that you suffer in

146
00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:16.580
reparation for others and in substitution for them and to give glory to God. So November

147
00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:29.700
24, 1903, how each word of Jesus is a link of grace. Continuing in my usual state, Louisa

148
00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:37.460
said, I saw blessed Jesus in my interior for just a little. And as if he wanted to continue

149
00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:46.620
removing doubts from me, he told me, daughter, I am the truth itself. That's John 14, six,

150
00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:54.260
I am the way the truth and the life. And falsehood could never come from me. At the most it is

151
00:18:54.260 --> 00:19:01.060
something that man does not understand. And I do this to show that if one does not understand

152
00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:09.700
God's word well, how can he understand the Creator? If we don't understand God's word,

153
00:19:09.700 --> 00:19:18.140
how can we understand him? However, the soul must respond by putting my word into practice.

154
00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:26.960
In fact, my words are many links of grace that come out of me and are given to the soul as a gift.

155
00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:34.780
Now, if she responds, she connects these links to the others, which she has already acquired. But

156
00:19:34.780 --> 00:19:41.780
if she doesn't respond, she sends them back to her Creator. Now, first of all, I want to give you

157
00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:48.620
the letter of James, chapter one, verses 21 and 22, where St. James tells us that we must not just

158
00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:55.500
read or listen to the word, we must put it into practice. Otherwise, it will do nothing but be

159
00:19:55.500 --> 00:20:06.980
our judge. The second one is Matthew 10, 13. That whatever we don't receive, it will go back to

160
00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:14.700
the Lord himself. Not only this, but Jesus said, I speak only when I see that the soul has the

161
00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:19.620
capacity to receive the gift. In other words, the Lord doesn't throw his pearls before swine.

162
00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:27.500
And if we like the swine, are only interested in worldly things and in slop and in muddy stuff and

163
00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:33.820
all the rest of it, he's not going to waste his pearls on us. So if the Lord is not communicating

164
00:20:33.820 --> 00:20:40.980
his divine word to us, then it means that we're actually not open to receive it. Let me read this

165
00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:48.660
again. Not only this, but I speak only when I see that the soul has the capacity to receive the

166
00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:56.620
gift. And responding to me, she acquires not only many links of grace, but also many links of

167
00:20:56.620 --> 00:21:05.540
divine wisdom. Now, it is extremely important for us to know that when the church tells us the seven

168
00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:11.300
signs of somebody in a relationship with God, the first one is wisdom, wisdom, understanding,

169
00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:18.180
counsel, fortitude, knowledge, piety, and the fear of the Lord. The first one is wisdom. If wisdom

170
00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:23.460
is not growing in us, then we're not growing in relationship with God, because he is eternal

171
00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:34.060
wisdom. And every touch of his adds wisdom to us. And so he continues and Jesus says, if I see all

172
00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:42.140
these graces linked with response, then the soul disposes me to give her yet more gifts. So what

173
00:21:42.140 --> 00:21:47.980
he's saying is the more you respond, the more you get. Now, this is what he said in the gospel to him

174
00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:54.620
who has more will be given. And to him who has not even that which he has will be taken away. In other

175
00:21:54.620 --> 00:22:00.660
words, if we use the gifts and the graces that God gives to us, he multiplies them. If we don't use

176
00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:06.820
them, they diminish and they disappear. But if he has given us grace that we haven't used, then we

177
00:22:06.820 --> 00:22:16.460
have to answer for it before him. But if I see that my gifts are sent back, I withdraw and I keep

178
00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:27.500
silent. That's a very important statement. So December the 3rd, 1903, with the divine will, we are

179
00:22:27.500 --> 00:22:35.380
everything without it. We are nothing. This is a VIP message. Okay, make sure you write VIP on your

180
00:22:35.380 --> 00:22:44.820
page. Continuing in my usual state, my blessed Jesus came for just a little telling me, my daughter,

181
00:22:44.820 --> 00:22:54.340
any human action which has no connection with the divine will puts God out of his own creation. Now,

182
00:22:54.340 --> 00:23:01.580
he's telling us that whatever we do outside of the divine will is not only useless, it can be

183
00:23:01.580 --> 00:23:08.020
sinful, but it's not only useless, but it keeps God out of his creation. Because God works through

184
00:23:08.020 --> 00:23:17.420
his divine will, in us and in all things, even suffering itself as holy, noble and precious as it

185
00:23:17.420 --> 00:23:23.460
might be before my eyes. If it is not a birth from my will, in other words, if it hasn't come from

186
00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:30.820
the divine will, instead of pleasing me, it makes me indignant and is disgusting to me. Or the power

187
00:23:30.820 --> 00:23:41.220
of the will of God, how holy, adorable and lovable you are. With you, we are everything, Philippians

188
00:23:41.220 --> 00:23:50.980
4, 13, even if we did nothing, because your will is fertile and it gives birth to all goods for us.

189
00:23:50.980 --> 00:23:59.020
Without you, we are nothing. That's literally a quotation from John 15, 5, where Jesus says,

190
00:23:59.020 --> 00:24:06.940
"Without me, you can do nothing." So, without you, we are nothing even if we did everything,

191
00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:15.900
because the human will is sterile and makes everything sterile. Now, here again, we come to a vital point

